WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.840
It was this price a second ago. Why is my bill different?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.643
The last price on screen is a record of the most recent trade.

00:00:12.643 --> 00:00:14.668
It's not an offer for unlimited size.

00:00:14.668 --> 00:00:18.390
How much people want to buy and sell right now is in the order book.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.747
Say you buy 0. 002 bitcoin. The first level only has half.

00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:43.260
The other half fills at a higher price. Together, the average is 50,050, not 50,000.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.126
Slippage is the gap between the price you expected and the price you got.

00:01:04.126 --> 00:01:07.524
It isn't always against you. The trading fee is a separate cost.

00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:10.020
Don't lump them together under a 'free' slogan.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.004
Bigger orders,

00:01:25.004 --> 00:01:29.903
thinner depth or fast markets make it more likely the result drifts from what you expected.

00:01:29.903 --> 00:01:33.780
Check size and depth before you order, and the real average price after.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:43.740
No.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.980
You only know your fill when you see the bill. Don't just watch the biggest number.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.842
Fees are one cost you can actually lower. Compare fees on NexuAlpha,

00:01:59.842 --> 00:02:05.018
and register through an official partner link with our code to get part of your trading fees back.

00:02:05.018 --> 00:02:06.180
Lower cost, same risk.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:10.092
You placed a buy order and nothing happens. Is it broken?

00:02:10.092 --> 00:02:11.910
Next: market, limit and cancel.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.430
Understand first, then act.
